# Run-wide xfails of mortar by architecture (spec/harness.md "Markers"):
# mortar has no back end there yet, so every mortar link of the
# architecture is expected to fail. One line per architecture:
#
#   mortar,<arch>: <reason>
#
# It takes the place of a test's own xfail(mortar) on that architecture
# (a test's skip still applies). A mortar link that passes is XPASS, so
# the line goes when the back end lands.

# Every x86-64 link is refused (crates/mortar/src/front.rs, "linking for
# x86-64").
mortar,x86_64: mortar: x86-64 back end is WP-029b stage B

# No i386 back end.
mortar,i386: mortar: i386 back end is WP-030 stage 2
